cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Algorithm or Skill? A calibrated Monte Carlo model of creator strategy and emergent inequality on TikTok"
message: "If you use this model or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Maan
    given-names: Rayyan
repository-code: "https://github.com/rayyanmaan/tiktok-creator-strategy-simulation"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based Monte Carlo simulation of a short-video recommendation
  platform, calibrated from four real datasets, used to test whether creator
  strategy (niche consistency, trend chasing, quality investment, or random
  posting) meaningfully changes follower outcomes, virality, and inequality.
keywords:
  - monte-carlo
  - agent-based-modelling
  - recommender-systems
  - complex-systems
  - inequality
  - gini-coefficient
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-04-23"
